<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wartislaw IX, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1400–<a href="/years/1457">1457</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wartislaw IX was duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania-wolgast">Pomerania-Wolgast</a>, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a>, from the 1410s until his death in 1457. He supported the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-greifswald">University of Greifswald</a> in 1456 by the burgomaster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heinrich-rubenow">Heinrich Rubenow</a>, one of the oldest universities of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. During his reign the Pomeranian duchies were drawn into conflicts with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and the Hanseatic towns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wartislaw-ix-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Wartislaw IX, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joachim Albrecht Holtzerlandt (um 1719-1805) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pommersches_Landesmuseum-Herzog_Wartislaw_IX_von_Pommern-Wolgast-WUS08658.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
